Nscale release v1.2.1-rc2-nscale.1
===================================

This branch, `release/v1.2.1-nscale`, is the Nscale build of Agent Router (Envoy AI Gateway) v1.2.1-rc2. It is
upstream's v1.2 patch series plus fixes the fork needs that upstream has not released on v1.2 yet.

Release tag: `nscale/v1.2.1-rc2-nscale.1`. Pushing the tag runs `.github/workflows/release.yaml`, which publishes:

| Artifact          | Location                                                           |
|-------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Controller image  | `registry.nscale.com/envir/ai-gateway-controller:v1.2.1-rc2-nscale.1` |
| Extproc image     | `registry.nscale.com/envir/ai-gateway-extproc:v1.2.1-rc2-nscale.1`    |
| Helm chart        | `oci://registry.nscale.com/helm-charts/ai-gateway-helm`, version `v1.2.1-rc2-nscale.1` |
| CRDs Helm chart   | `oci://registry.nscale.com/helm-charts/ai-gateway-crds-helm`, version `v1.2.1-rc2-nscale.1` |
| GitHub release    | Draft release on the tag, with the charts and `aigw` binaries attached |

Images carry the `org.opencontainers.image.revision` label with the commit they were built from. The chart is
rewritten to point at the Harbor images before it is packaged.


How the branch is built
-----------------------

The branch is four layers. Commit SHAs are on this branch; "from" gives the commit it was cherry-picked from
(`git cherry-pick -x` records it in each commit message).

```
upstream release/v1.2 (v1.2.1-rc2, 45ccd9fe)
  + fork CI                      4 commits, from the fork's main
  + upstream main-only fixes     8 commits, from upstream main
  + embedding passthrough fixes  9 commits, the fork's own
  + release tag format           1 commit
```


1. Base: upstream v1.2.1-rc2
----------------------------

Upstream `release/v1.2` at `45ccd9fe` ("envoy 1.39.6"), tagged `v1.2.1-rc2`. Over v1.2.0 it adds:

- The MCP proxy listens on `127.0.0.1` only. It used to bind every interface, so any pod that could reach port
  9856 could set the headers Envoy sets after enforcing the MCPRoute security policy, and skip that policy.
- Malformed 2xx upstream responses (Anthropic without `usage`, null Gemini, image generation or Bedrock Converse
  bodies) no longer panic the external processor.
- MCP session IDs work only on the MCPRoute that created them.
- `promptSelector` is enforced on `prompts/get` and `completion/complete`.
- The controller reads at most 1 MiB of an MCPRoute's OAuth authorization server metadata.
- MCP session encryption seeds are delivered in the filter config Secret instead of as command-line arguments,
  so they no longer appear in Pod specs.
- Debug logs redact `api-key` and `x-amz-security-token`, and header mutations in immediate responses.
- Controller replicas retry on conflict when patching the admission webhook's `caBundle`.
- Go 1.27.3 and Envoy Proxy 1.39.6.

Upstream's own notes are in `release-notes/v1.2.1.md`. Upgrading from v1.2.0 rolls Gateway pods that serve
MCPRoutes once, and an MCP session ID reused on a different MCPRoute now returns 400.


2. Fork CI
----------

These make CI publish to Harbor from `nscale/v*` tags and turn off the jobs that only work in the upstream
repository. The workflow files match the fork's `main`, except for the tag format change in layer 4.

| Commit     | From       | Change |
|------------|------------|--------|
| `e1201e6d` | `0378a7a6` | Gate upstream-only workflows (Codecov, image and chart pushes on branch pushes) |
| `fbab7528` | `b0777d9e` | Publish images and charts to Harbor instead of GHCR |
| `ae4178db` | `38e53aea` | Finish partial GitHub releases on re-run. The upstream-sync workflow from this commit is left out |
| `bd92cbdb` | `4a46575f` | Log in to Harbor for charts with the repository's chart robot |


