| Commit     | From       | Change |
|------------|------------|--------|
| `d086ad4a` | `f2a14b7c` | Add Claude Sonnet 5.5 to the structured output and effort model list |
| `5ee7bfe5` | `31ee356f` | Add one InferencePool ext proc filter per pool, not per route match |
| `547b6fc3` | `35307e5e` | Keep Anthropic streaming overload errors in-band |
| `e1435c1e` | `ffdb12ea` | Apply QuotaPolicy changes to the Envoy config without a restart |
| `0b5a5e48` | `81c3ccc4` | Stop charging a quota hit at request time |
| `1ccbb632` | `1c98cc80` | Add Claude Haiku 5.5 to the structured output and effort model list |
| `19e0c102` | `f89fa2b3` | Keep the query string on Anthropic passthrough |
| `4e2a8f8f` | `76f60022` | Forward ping events on the AWS Anthropic messages path |


4. Embedding passthrough fixes
------------------------------

The fork's fixes for memory use on OpenAI and Azure OpenAI embedding passthrough, proposed upstream from the
`fix/embedding-passthrough-memory-upstream` branch. The "From" column is that branch.

| Commit     | From       | Change |
|------------|------------|--------|
| `91b5d861` | `9be4dd4c` | Escape user-facing error JSON |
| `0e1ae3b1` | `f81a7760` | Avoid decoding vectors in embeddings passthrough |
| `ef0cd586` | `8b0619fa` | Keep case-sensitive embedding metadata decoding |
| `3ad169d4` | `c7f4947e` | Make embedding trace capture best effort |
| `8a92427d` | `9a14104c` | Make embedding vector validation configurable |
| `ad778cb4` | `a90b9f3e` | Make passthrough embedding trace vectors optional |
| `3b701726` | `19cd7a1d` | Document embedding validation and trace memory costs |
| `b5c76d26` | `5a1b7ac8` | Drop the generated chart README |
| `c84045b4` | `91a49be9` | Use the chart's comment style for the embedding values |

Both new settings default to `true`, which keeps upstream behaviour. To cut embedding memory use, turn them off
in the chart values:

```yaml
extProc:
  # Validate vectors in embedding responses. With false, only JSON syntax and model/usage are validated.
  # A 100 MiB response benchmark allocated about 2.66 GiB with validation, versus 256 MiB without it.
  validateEmbeddingVectors: false
  # Capture vectors in traces. Only applies when validateEmbeddingVectors is false.
  traceEmbeddingVectors: false
```

| Chart value                        | Controller flag                      | Extproc flag                |
|------------------------------------|--------------------------------------|-----------------------------|
| `extProc.validateEmbeddingVectors` | `--extProcValidateEmbeddingVectors`  | `-validateEmbeddingVectors` |
| `extProc.traceEmbeddingVectors`    | `--extProcTraceEmbeddingVectors`     | `-traceEmbeddingVectors`    |

The controller passes the extproc flags only when they are `false`, so deployments that keep the defaults are not
rolled on upgrade. The full description is in `site/docs/capabilities/gateway-config.md` and
`site/docs/capabilities/observability/tracing.md`.


5. Release tag format
---------------------

`2d0eb196` lets `release.yaml` accept a tag built on an upstream release candidate. Tags must match
`nscale/v<major>.<minor>.<patch>[-rc<m>]-nscale.<n>`, for example `nscale/v1.2.0-nscale.1` or
`nscale/v1.2.1-rc2-nscale.1`.


Not included
------------

Upstream `main` also has features after v1.2.0 that this branch leaves out: dynamic, weekly, monthly and yearly
quota windows, cross-namespace quota backends, the OpenAI decision API, OpenAI workload identity federation, and
the removal of the unused `GCPWorkloadIdentityProvider` API type. It also leaves out docs, site and test-only
changes.


Cutting the next release
------------------------

When upstream tags the final v1.2.1, or later v1.2 patches, rebuild the branch on the new upstream `release/v1.2`
and reapply layers 2 to 5. Drop any layer 3 commit that upstream has backported, and any layer 4 commit that
upstream has merged. Then increment the `-nscale.<n>` number, or reset it to 1 for a new upstream version, and
update this file.
